From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Claude Opus 5.5" <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 00:00:07 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 19/25] No LibVLC: audio and video through CEF; licenses for
 what ships

VLC is GPL, so the Windows build and package leave out the LibVLC media
plugin and VLC's libraries (and the example plugin), and nothing in the
build needs the vlc-bin package any more. The media types LibVLC played
(parcel music, audio and video URLs) go to the CEF plugin, whose
Chromium plays the common formats; RTSP and formats Chromium can't
decode don't play. About no longer lists a LibVLC version.

licenses.txt drops software Ibasho doesn't include (the Logitech LCD SDK,
FSI FontShop's Meta fonts, glh, Kakadu's JPEG2000, xmlrpc-epi,
google-perftools) and adds OpenJPEG's license. The About box's Licenses
tab says Linden Lab's copyright line is for the viewer Ibasho is built on.
